Two fields the lens would copy into ones that do not accept every value of
them: one diagnostic at the lens, whose help names both, with each field's
reason as a note.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	id:    string
	count: int
	limit: int
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	id:    string
	count: int & <10
	limit: int & >0
	owner: string
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		owner: "nobody"
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	id:    string
	count: int & <10
	limit: int & >0
	owner: string
}
-- out/error --
error[E0358]: the ForwardLens of v1.0 would copy v0_0.count and v0_0.limit into count and limit, which do not accept every value of them
 --> history/1.0.thema:8:1
  |
8 | ForwardLens: {
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = note: both v0.0 and v1.0 declare count and limit, so a lens that does not map them copies them
  = note: count in v1.0 is now int & <10, which does not accept every value of the prior int
  = note: limit in v1.0 is now int & >0, which does not accept every value of the prior int
  = help: map count and limit in the ForwardLens, each with a _match, a computed value, or a constant
